el/pull/567"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/issues/567"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/issues/567/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/pulls/567/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/pulls/567/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/statuses/79660bba3b414c37328235214e4401644939921e"}},"author_association":"NONE","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/pulls/560","id":4435173700,"node_id":"PR_kwDOFNE1eM8AAAABCFthRA","html_url":"https://github.com/driftingly/rector-laravel/pull/560","diff_url":"https://github.com/driftingly/rector-laravel/pull/560.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/driftingly/rector-laravel/pull/560.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/driftingly/rector-laravel/issues/560","number":560,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add CommandPropertyToAsCommandAttributeRector","user":{"login":"chinmaypurav","id":70144052,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTQ0MDUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70144052?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav","html_url":"https://github.com/chinmaypurav","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chinmaypurav/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #383.\n\nMoves a console command's `$signature`/`$name` and `$description` into Symfony's `#[AsCommand]`.\n\n```diff\n use Illuminate\\Console\\Command;\n+use Symfony\\Component\\Console\\Attribute\\AsCommand;\n\n+#[AsCommand(name: 'mail:send', description: 'Send the queued emails')]\n class SendEmails extends Command\n {\n-    protected $signature = 'mail:send';\n-\n-    protected $description = 'Send the queued emails';\n }\n```\n\n### Why this is behaviour preserving\n\nSymfony's `Command` declares `$name`, `$description`, `$help` and `$hidden` as **private**, so Laravel's `protected` redeclarations occupy separate slots. Symfony's constructor reads the attribute into its own slots, and Laravel's constructor only overwrites them when its own properties are non-empty. Removing the properties therefore hands control to the attribute — for `$signature`, `$name` and `$description`.\n\n`$help`, `$hidden` and `$aliases` are deliberately left in place: the `help` argument needs Symfony Console 7.3, and Laravel's constructor unconditionally overwrites help and hidden from its own properties, so moving those would be a behaviour change.\n\n### The signature problem\n\nAs raised in the issue, a signature carrying arguments or options can't be expressed as an attribute name, since Laravel parses the input definition out of it. Those are skipped.\n\nRelated, and easy to miss: dropping `$signature` makes Laravel call `specifyParameters()`, which reactivates `getArguments()`/`getOptions()`. The rule skips classes that override either, checked through the inheritance chain via reflection rather than just the class body.\n\n### Other cases skipped\n\nSignatures with whitespace or `|` alias pipes; classes declaring both `$signature` and `$name` (the signature silently wins, so that's a human's call); abstract and anonymous classes; an existing `#[AsCommand]`; non-`protected`, `static`, `readonly` or grouped (`$a = 'x', $b = 'y'`) properties; non-literal defaults; empty signatures; and classes reading `$this->signature`/`$this->description` in their own body.\n\n### Cases handled rather than skipped\n\n`$description = ''` — property dropped, argument omitted, since that's the default anyway. A non-literal `$description` next to a literal signature — the name is converted and the description property stays put. `$name` alongside `getArguments()` — safe, because `specifyParameters()` already runs on that path. Existing attribute groups are appended to.\n\n### Notes\n\nGated on `laravel/framework >=9.0` (`AsCommand` needs Symfony Console 6+) and `PhpVersionFeature::ATTRIBUTES`.\n\nI left the rule out of every set on purpose — it isn't tied to a Laravel version bump, and it would collide with the Laravel 13 `#[Signature]`/`#[Description]` rules if both ran. Happy to add it wherever you'd prefer.\n\n26 fixtures (8 transforming, 18 skip). PHPStan max, duster and structarmed are clean, docs regenerated. The suite has 8 failures on `main` already, all in `ArrayDimFetch`/`ReplaceFakerInstanceWithHelperRector` and unrelated to this change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-09-03T17:07:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T05:34:31Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ff95e2682bdbe198652593a4980b501943caeec5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"calebdw","id":4176520,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzY1MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4176520?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/calebdw","html_url":"https://github.com/calebdw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calebdw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/calebdw/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/